# api-live-evaluation

**Outdated (2026-10-23):** the student sees the written result on save, and rank updates on that save. The save is a draft until the Master Admin publishes.

`INSTRUCTOR` is created like a System Admin: no password on create, activation code, the instructor sets the password. One instructor per module. A System Admin does not evaluate. The Master Admin may evaluate any written paper.

A save needs marks from 0 through the maximum and an evaluated PDF. The comment is optional. The student sees the result on save and never sees the evaluator. A later save replaces the file and recalculates rank.

The MCQ live leaderboard opens five minutes after the window and lists live participants only. A no-submit written row is visible and cannot be marked.

Slice 2: the instructor browses assigned modules only and downloads the answer PDF. A System Admin can read the evaluator name and cannot mark. A comment is shown to the student when one was entered. A written retake is marked and stays off the live board. The submission list shows the deadline post.
